   "file": "apps/web/lib/site.ts",
   "fp": "a86a3c8eca7a",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 24,
   "message": "`knownOrigin` rewrites `baseUrl`'s conditions so it can guess when `baseUrl` will succeed: `AMAX_BASE_URL` set, or not production and a loopback host. That is a second copy of the origin rule. Today they agree because both use `LOOPBACK`. If `baseUrl` ever accepts a different set of hosts, `knownOrigin` will still call it and it will throw, or it will return null where `baseUrl` would have given an origin. Fix: keep the rule in one place. For example, have `baseUrl` call a shared `resolveOrigin(h): string | null`, throw when that returns null, and have `knownOrigin` return its result directly.",
   "original_severity": "minor",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B4",
   "scenario": "No current input shows a wrong result, because both copies use the same `LOOPBACK` regex.",
   "severity": "minor"
  },
  {
   "file": "apps/web/components/marketing/ProductVideo.tsx",
